            {"title": "Memory by thread_id, and a human approval step (runs offline)", "language": "python", "runnable": True,
             "code": "import operator\nfrom typing import Annotated, TypedDict\nfrom langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver\nfrom langgraph.graph import END, START, StateGraph\nfrom langgraph.types import Command, interrupt\n\n# 1) Memory: the same thread_id continues, a new one starts fresh\nclass Chat(TypedDict):\n    turns: Annotated[list, operator.add]\n\nchat = StateGraph(Chat)\nchat.add_node('reply', lambda s: {'turns': ['reply']})\nchat.add_edge(START, 'reply')\nchat.add_edge('reply', END)\napp = chat.compile(checkpointer=MemorySaver())\n\nfor thread in ['alice', 'alice', 'bob']:\n    out = app.invoke({'turns': ['user']}, {'configurable': {'thread_id': thread}})\n    print(thread, out['turns'])\n\n# 2) Human in the loop: pause, then resume with the human's decision\nclass Refund(TypedDict):\n    amount: int\n    status: str\n\ndef ask_human(state):\n    approved = interrupt({'question': f\"Approve refund of {state['amount']}?\"})\n    return {'status': 'refunded' if approved else 'rejected'}\n\nrefund = StateGraph(Refund)\nrefund.add_node('ask_human', ask_human)\nrefund.add_edge(START, 'ask_human')\nrefund.add_edge('ask_human', END)\napp2 = refund.compile(checkpointer=MemorySaver())\n\ncfg = {'configurable': {'thread_id': 'refund-1'}}\npaused = app2.invoke({'amount': 5000, 'status': 'pending'}, cfg)\nprint('paused with:', paused['__interrupt__'][0].value)\nprint('next node :', app2.get_state(cfg).next)\nprint('resumed   :', app2.invoke(Command(resume=True), cfg))\n",
             "expected_output": "alice ['user', 'reply']\nalice ['user', 'reply', 'user', 'reply']\nbob ['user', 'reply']\npaused with: {'question': 'Approve refund of 5000?'}\nnext node : ('ask_human',)\nresumed   : {'amount': 5000, 'status': 'refunded'}",
             "explain": [{"lines": "7-18", "text": "Compile with a MemorySaver. The list state has a reducer, so each call APPENDS."}, {"lines": "20-22", "text": "'alice' called twice sees her earlier turns; 'bob' starts with an empty history. Real apps must derive thread_id from the authenticated user."}, {"lines": "25-31", "text": "interrupt() pauses the run and hands a question to the caller."}, {"lines": "40-44", "text": "The first invoke stops at the interrupt (the saved state says the next node is ask_human). Command(resume=True) continues, and interrupt() returns True inside the node."}]},
